{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review and fund more support for care leavers",
        "additional_details": "A new review shows that young adults who have left care have a death rate around four times higher than the general population. Just over a third of the care leavers were thought to have died by suicide.\r\n \r\nWe want the Government to fund a national care leaver mental health and suicide-prevention programme, informed by the 2026 review and care leaver death rates. This should provide local support groups, a dedicated mental health worker alongside each care leaver\u2019s PA, and access to specialist support. Care leavers need a clear, funded pathway to help. Government should also fund consistent national reporting of care-leaver deaths and suspected suicides.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to introduce a national suicide prevention and wellbeing standard, ensuring care leavers have continuous support through the transition to adulthood. ",
